      "title": "List_of_political_parties_in_Nasastan",
      "categories": [
        "Political_parties",
        "Nasastan"
      ],
      "snippet": "{{Politics of Nasastan}}\n\nThe [[Nasastan|National Federation of Nasastan]] is a federal parliamentary authoritarian republic characterized by a political system of [[Guided democracy|managed pluralism]]. Under the [[Constitution of Nasastan|Constitution of 1937]], political participation is structured through a unique asymmetric bicameral legislature that separates economic governance from sociocultural deliberation. While the country permits a degree of multiparty competition, the [[Ethnofederalist Social Nasastani National Party]] (SNNSP) functions as the dominant legal and administrative framework of the state. Political activity in Nasastan is divided according to the specific competencies of the two parliamentary chambers; The [[Purokal]] (Economic Chamber)''':''' Membership is strictly restricted to representatives of the SNNSP. Economic debate is not conducted between rival parties but within five internal ideological factions of the SNNSP, which range from far-left to far-right economic currents. The [[Rada]] (Sociocultural Chamber) operates under a system of full party plurality, serving as the primary forum for multiparty competition and ideological contestation. Despite the plurality found in the Rada, all sociocultural legislation is subject to the absolute veto of the [[Načelnik]], the cultural sentinel of the state. Consequently, political parties in Nasastan function less as sovereign lawmaking bodies and more as mechanisms for regulating political participatio"
    },
