      "snippet": "{{Urcea WIP}}\n{{OOD}}\n{{Infobox political party |name = Union for National Solidarity |logo = |leader = [[Livio Iarnán]] |founder = [[James Cossus Reed]] |founded = {{start date|2015|10|26}} |preceded_by = [[Commonwealth Union (Urcea)|Commonwealth Union]] |headquarters = 698 Impireachtor Street, [[Urcepól (City)|Urcepól]], [[Urcea]] |ideology =\n\n[[Wittonian Socialism]]\n[[Organicism]] |religion = [[Levantine Catholic Church|Catholicism]] |colors = Tyrian purple }}\nThe '''Union for National Solidarity''' is one of the three major contemporary [[Political parties in Urcea|political parties]] in [[Urcea]], along with the its rival, the [[Social Labor Party (Urcea)|Social Labor Party]] as well as the [[National Pact (Urcea)|National Pact]]. The Union's history originates in the Crown Regency of [[Gréagóir FitzRex]], whose policies and inclinations led to the creation of the [[Commonwealth Union (Urcea)|Commonwealth Union]], the UNS's legal predecessor. The ideology of the Union was especially shaped by the policies of the [[Michael Witte|Witte]] administration, policies that formed the ideological basis of [[Wittonian Socialism]]. The Union is the third largest party in the [[Conshilía Daoni]], inheriting the remnant delegates of the National Social Union.\n\n== History ==\n{{Main|Commonwealth Union (Urcea)}}\nCommonwealth Union survived as a united entity until the ascension of [[James Cossus Reed]] as Witte's successor. The failure of Reed's policies combined with the internal press"
