      "categories": [
        "League_of_Nations"
      ],
      "snippet": "{{wip}}\n\n{{Infobox military award\n|name= League of Nations Service Medal\n|image=Varshan Service Medal.png\n|caption= League of Nations Service Medal\n|image2=[[File:MY-TER Family Order of Terengganu 1st class - DK I.svg|border|120px]] \n|caption2=Service ribbon\n|presenter= {{flag|League of Nations}}\n|type= {{wp|Campaign medal}}\n|eligibility= All [[League of Nations Command]] forces\n|awarded_for= Campaign service\n|campaign= [[Final War of the Deluge]]\n|status= \n|description=\n|clasps=\n|established= 14 September 2025\n|firstawarded=\n|lastawarded=\n|total_awarded= \n|total_awarded_posthumously=\n|total_recipients=\n|individual=\n|higher=\n|same=\n|lower= \n|related= \n}}\n\nThe '''League of Nations Service Medal''' ('''LoNM''') is an {{wp|international military decoration}} established by the [[League of Nations]] on September 14, 2025. The decoration is the first international award ever created by the League of Nations and recognized the multi-national defense forces which participated in the [[Final War of the Deluge]] in combat operations against [[Varshan]].\n\n==Criteria==\n\nEligibility for the Service Medal is used as a criteria for eligibility for grants under the [[League of Nations Wartime Benefit Fund]].\n\n==Description==\n\n==Prominent recipients==\n*{{flagicon|Urcea}} [[Martin St. Clair]], Supreme Allied Commander Varshan, [[League of Nations Command]]\n*{{flagicon|Urcea}} [[Aedan Frantone]], Lec. Pri, [[Royal and Imperial Army (Urcea)|Royal and Imperial Army]]\n*{{flagicon|Daxia}} [[Bort B"
    },
    {
      "title": "League_of_Nations_Wartime_Benefit_Fund",
      "categories": [
        "League_of_Nations"
      ],
      "snippet": "{{stub}}\n\nThe '''League of Nations Wartime Benefit Fund''' is a fund established by the [[Treaty of Electorsbourg (2024)|Treaty of Electorsbourg]] intended to benefit the orphans and widows of [[League of Nations Command]] soldiers during the [[Final War of the Deluge]]. The fund was created using the proceeds from sales of military and other equipment captured from [[Varshan]] at the end of the war, particularly warships. The fund, established under the auspices of the [[Provost-General of the League of Nations]], coordinated with participating nations to establish benefit programs on the national level with which the Fund provides block grant funding. While most criteria is established at the national level, the Fund requires that benefit be provided to the spouses of or children of service members who are eligible for the [[League of Nations Service Medal]] and who died in the line of service.\n\n[[Category: The Deluge]]\n[[Category: League of Nations]]"
    },
