      "title": "Model_League_of_Nations",
      "categories": [
        "League_of_Nations"
      ],
      "snippet": "'''Model League of Nations (MLoN)''' is an education simulation of various committee meetings based off real-life committee meetings of the [[League of Nations]] (LoN). These meetings are typically extracurricular, centered around political science programs and diplomatic education. MLoN was first popularized in [[Porlos]] following the country's independence in the 1940s, along with the signing of the [[Code of the League of Nations|League of Nations Treaty]] in 1955, and quickly spread in across the rest of [[South Crona]] over the course of the next two decades. As of now, MLoN is one of the most popular extracurricular activities in university settings, with students typically representing all of the LoN member states in several simulated committees.\n\n(Will work on this over the next week i need to go to sleep becasue I have church tomorrow)\n\n== History ==\n\nSimulations of LoN meetings began in [[Porlos]], with the establishment of\n\n[[Category:IXWB]]\n[[Category:League of Nations]]"
