    {
      "title": "Holy_League",
      "categories": [
        "Alliances"
      ],
      "snippet": "{{stub}}\n\nThe '''Holy League''' was a coalition of [[Catholic Church|Catholic]] members within the [[Holy Levantine Empire]] during the mid-16th century who were joined together for the purposes of defending the Empire generally and the Catholic ascendancy within it specifically. Unlike its opposition, the [[Protestant Union]], the Holy League had no central leadership but was a coalition of many different members of the [[Kingdom of Dericania]] and principalities within future [[Fiannria]]. The Holy League was established in response to the creation of the [[Protestant Union]] as a way to coordinate the Catholic war effort during the [[Great Confessional War]] and protect the lands and territories of its constituent members. It was dissolved with the Catholic victory during the Great Confessional War, and its members - especially those founding families and princes of the League - benefitted from the war greatly, gaining the lands and territories of disinherited {{wp|Protestant}} lords.\n\n[[Category: Alliances]]\n[[Category:IXWB]]"
    },
    {
      "title": "Latin_League",
      "categories": [
        "Alliances"
      ],
      "snippet": "{{stub}}\n\nThe '''Latin League''' was a coalition of [[Latinic people|Latinic]] successor states and city-states following the collapse of central authority of [[Great Levantia]] in the beginning of the 6th century. The League was established in the 670s for the purposes of mutual defense against [[Gothic people|Goths]] to the north, [[Gallawa]] to the east, and later [[Uzdehzanistan]] to the south. The [[Urcepól (Duchy)|Duchy of Urcepól]] and [[Harren#Independent_Ducal_period|Duchy of Hortia]], the [[Kingdom of Pumbria]], and the duchies of [[Urcea Maritima]] were among its most prominent members. It was destroyed in the 750s by [[Conchobar I, Emperor of the Levantines|Conchobar]], King of Gallawa, whose control of the former Latin heartland would empower him to form the [[Holy Levantine Empire|Levantine Empire]] shortly after its demise. The lands of most of these cities and polities were reorganized into the [[Urcepól (Archduchy)|Archduchy of Urcepól]], [[Harren|Duchy of Harren]], and the various [[Creagmer republics]] of the western coast. It is generally believed that [[vigintiquinque]] affiliation played an extensive role in the internal politics of the League, though many of the intricacies of how the League was divided are not understood by modern historians.\n\nUrcepólic Duke [[Gaius Julius Cicurinus]] rose to prominence in the mid-8th century at the head of Latin League forces against both Uzdehzanistan and Gallawa, using politics, Celtic integration, and clever tactic"
    },
